From 5d84e32c18e60dd65d7eadf88264bfb494eea045 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The browser Authors <noreply@browser.invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:12:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/61] cursor-overlay

CDP screencast cursor overlay compositing. Its page_handler.cc/.h wiring
rides in agent-snapshot, which dominates that file; its BUILD.gn sources and
input_handler member ride in keyboard-typing.

One overlay per tab (WebContentsUserData), redrawn through DevToolsVideoConsumer::RequestRefreshFrame; the frame-stream's change callback rides in devtools_video_consumer.*; video-recording's lines in cdp_cursor_overlay.h/.cc ride here too (a recording draws the CDP cursor into its frames): DrawCursor, which screencast frames and recordings share; RenderSprite; ForRecording, the overlay a recording makes without --show-cdp-cursor, which tracks the pointer and draws nothing on the window (draws_on_window); and the pointer's position, look version and click count, which a recording reads.
---
